        "input": {
          "ruleId": "INDEMN",
          "level": "preferred",
          "summary": "Broaden Garman indemnity beyond IP title and soften notice condition",
          "comment": "[Playbook] The Section 13 indemnity covers only breach of the IP ownership warranty; we need the standard additional heads (breach of law, data compromise, gross negligence/wilful misconduct) and a notice provision that only bites where Garman is prejudiced.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "insert_after",
              "paragraphId": "p0093",
              "text": "Garman shall further defend, indemnify and hold harmless Sparkling and its affiliates from and against any third-party claim, and all resulting Losses, to the extent arising out of (a) Garman's breach of applicable law; (b) any unauthorised access to or disclosure of Sparkling's data caused by Garman; or (c) Garman's gross negligence or wilful misconduct. Sparkling's failure to give notice of a claim within ten calendar days shall not relieve Garman of its obligations except to the extent Garman is materially prejudiced thereby."
            }
          ]
        },
