          "level": "fallback",
          "summary": "Convert no-hire into narrow non-solicit with advertising carve-out",
          "comment": "[Playbook] We cannot accept a no-hire covering all employees of the other party. We have narrowed Section 19 to a non-solicit of personnel actually involved in the services, with the usual general-advertising and unsolicited-approach carve-outs.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0133",
              "oldText": "both parties agree not to hire or allow its respective affiliates to hire any employee of the other party, or any person who was an employee of the other party during the previous six months and who was directly involved in the provision of services under this Agreement.",
              "newText": "both parties agree not to solicit for employment any person who is or was an employee of the other party directly involved in the provision of services under this Agreement, provided that this restriction shall not apply to general advertisements or recruitment efforts not specifically targeted at such persons, or to unsolicited approaches by such persons, and shall not prohibit either party from hiring any such person."
